<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eisenach</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eisenach is a town in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, at the edge of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringian-forest">Thuringian Forest</a>, below the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wartburg">Wartburg</a> castle. It was a residence of the Ludowingian landgraves of Thuringia and later the capital of the Duchy of Saxe-Eisenach. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Martin Luther</a> went to school there, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johann-sebastian-bach">Johann Sebastian Bach</a> was born there in 1685, and in 1869 the Social Democratic Workers' Party was founded in the town.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eisenach.jpg" alt="Eisenach" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Westerdam · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eisenach_von_G%C3%B6pelskuppe.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
